## QA / E2E

This store has automated E2E coverage of the purchase journey (home → PLP → PDP → cart → checkout), driven by [`@decocms/qa`](https://github.com/decocms/qa).

### Locally

```sh
# Against your dev server (default: http://localhost:8000)
bun run qa:local

# Against staging or a specific URL
./scripts/qa-local.sh https://staging.example.com

# Headless smoke run
bun run qa:smoke

# Report which data-qa-* markers a single page exposes (quick marker check)
bunx @decocms/qa doctor --url http://localhost:8000
```

The local run opens a real browser and pauses at each step so you can inspect the page. Useful when a CI run fails and you want to reproduce.

### In CI

- **PRs:** [`.github/workflows/qa-pr.yml`](./.github/workflows/qa-pr.yml) waits for the decobot preview comment, extracts the URL, and runs the journey against it. Result appears as a check named "Purchase journey".
- **main:** [`.github/workflows/qa-main.yml`](./.github/workflows/qa-main.yml) runs the journey against the production URL on every push to `main` and on manual dispatch.

Both workflows run a `qa doctor` **CORE-marker pre-step** before the journey: if an entry-page CORE marker (`data-qa-category-link` / `data-qa-cart-icon`) is missing on the target, the run fails immediately with the named marker instead of a cryptic mid-journey error.

### Adding coverage

The journey relies on `data-qa-*` attributes in the JSX. The canonical slugs are documented in the [engine README](https://github.com/decocms/qa#canonical-data-qa-attributes). To extend with a new slug:

1. Mark the element in this repo's JSX.
2. Open a PR on `@decocms/qa` to add the slug to the canonical list.

### Debugging a failed run

1. Open the failed workflow in GitHub Actions.
2. Download the `qa-output-*` artifact (contains screenshots + JSON report).
3. Re-run locally against the same URL: `./scripts/qa-local.sh <preview-url>`.

### Configuration

`.qarc.json` at the repo root:

| Field | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `url` | Production URL (used by the `main` workflow). |
| `cep` | Brazilian postal code (used for shipping calculation steps). |
| `viewports` | Which viewports to run — `desktop`, `mobile`, `tablet`. |
| `selectors` | Per-slug CSS selector overrides. Use sparingly — prefer marking the JSX. |
| `features` | Engine flags — e.g. `checkoutUrlPattern` (assert checkout by URL glob), `checkoutCrossOrigin`, `dismissOverlaysHeuristic`. |
